name: sim.changeEntityColor
description: Changes the color of an entity, and returns its original color. Currently only takes into account collections and shapes
luaSynopsis: list originalColorData = sim.changeEntityColor(int entityHandle, list newColor, int colorComponent = sim.colorcomponent_ambient_diffuse)
pythonSynopsis: map[] originalColorData = sim.changeEntityColor(int entityHandle, float[3] newColor, int colorComponent = sim.colorcomponent_ambient_diffuse)
inputs:
1. entityHandle: handle of a entity
2. newColor: array of 3 rgb values, each between 0.0 and 1.0
3. colorComponent: a color component
outputs:
1. originalColorData: original color data, to be used as argument with sim.restoreEntityColor
